{
  "description": "Hand-read reference values for 30 exams, used to measure indicator accuracy (spec AC8). Read visually by the Analyst from 4x enlarged map images; the Product Owner may spot-check. Each indicator holds the list of acceptable values (more than one only where the printed text is partly covered and cannot be read with certainty). null means 'not scored' because the value is hidden or unreadable (typically the bold maximum curvature, which is often partly covered by a marker). Field 'set': 'tuning' (20 exams, may be used while developing the recogniser) or 'holdout' (10 exams, must not be used for tuning; only for the final evaluation).",
